<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grimoald Alferanites</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1119">1119</a>–1132</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grimoald Alferanites was a citizen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> who seized power in the city in 1119, during the weak rule of the Norman duke William II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, and styled himself prince. He governed Bari as an independent lordship for over a decade. In 1132 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a> captured him and sent him prisoner to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, ending the principality.</p></div>
